      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gibraltar, Michigan was first settled in 1811 and officially platted on March 14, 1837 by the Gibralter & Flat Rock Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibraltar%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the British overseas territory of Gibraltar, a strategic fortress on the Iberian Peninsula.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.waynecountymi.gov/Government/Departments/Economic-Development/Our-Communities/Gibraltar",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the War of 1812, the Battle of Brownstown was fought on the site that is now Carlson High School.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofgibraltarmi.gov/gibraltar-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Gibraltar incorporated as a village in 1954 and became an autonomous city in 1961.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibraltar%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
